\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. News: Higher Wages Proposed For H-1B Visa Holders\b0\par\par\uc2 By Lauren Weber \par \uc2 328 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 March 2026\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A5\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Trump administration plans to require higher wages for foreign workers who come to the U.S. on visas for high-skilled employees, its latest move to discourage U.S. companies from hiring foreign nationals instead of American workers.\par \par \uc2 The rule, which the Labor Department proposed Thursday, would lift the minimum pay for software developers and other workers who come to the U.S. in the H-1B program and in several other visa categories. Pay floors for workers would rise 21% to 33%, depending on their experience, the Labor Department said in its proposal.\par \par \uc2 Critics for years have assailed the H-1B program, the main pathway for highly skilled foreign professionals to work in the U.S. and a popular tool among big tech companies who say they need the imported labor to offset worker shortages at home. Opponents argue that employers have abused the program by hiring foreign workers on the cheap instead of better-paid U.S. employees.\par \par \uc2 There's little evidence of a pay disparity in studies comparing workers with the same levels of education and experience, said Stuart Anderson, executive director of the National Foundation for American Policy, a research organization that argues in favor of skilled immigration to the U.S.\par \par \uc2 The proposed rule is virtually identical to one put forward at the end of President Trump's first term, Anderson added. The Biden administration subsequently dropped the effort.\par \par \uc2 Every March, the government conducts a lottery that decides who will receive the coveted 85,000 new visas available for the coming year. The Trump administration recently changed the lottery to give workers who would be paid higher salaries better odds. Companies file hundreds of thousands of petitions for the visas each year.\par \par \uc2 H-1B visas are also the primary route for international students who get U.S. degrees to be able to stay and work in the country.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020260327em3r00023\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
