\par\par \b \uc2 KKR\uc2 's Investment in Cooling Site Is Winner\b0\par\par\uc2 By Lauren Thomas \par \uc2 426 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 March 2026\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 KKR\uc2 's $4.75 billion sale of data-center cooling business \uc2 CoolIT\uc2  to \uc2 Ecolab\uc2  is poised to be one of the private-equity giant's most successful bets ever. \uc2 CoolIT\uc2 's employees are set to reap the rewards, too.\par \par \uc2 KKR\uc2  bought a majority stake in 2023 when \uc2 CoolIT\uc2  was valued at around $270 million. The firm is set to make roughly 15 times the equity it invested, executives told The Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 The transaction, announced last week, will represent one of the firm's top returning investments over the past 20 years. The others are \uc2 AppLovin\uc2 , Japan's \uc2 Kokusai Electric\uc2  and garage-door maker CHI Overhead Doors, the executives said.\par \par \uc2 Since \uc2 KKR\uc2  took control, \uc2 CoolIT\uc2 's revenue has roughly quadrupled. The business has more than doubled its workforce, expanded capacity and won over more large-scale cloud-service providers as customers, the executives said.\par \par \uc2 Based in Canada, \uc2 CoolIT\uc2  makes liquid-cooling systems used in data centers and supports artificial-intelligence infrastructure. The sector is fairly consolidated. Late last year, power-management company Eaton struck a nearly $10 billion deal for \uc2 Boyd\uc2 's thermal business, which makes similar liquid-cooling solutions.\par \par \uc2 When the sale to \uc2 Ecolab\uc2  closes, \uc2 CoolIT\uc2 's roughly 640 employees are each expected to receive average payouts of around $240,000. The longest-serving employees could receive payouts of at least $380,000, or eight times their salaries, \uc2 KKR\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 KKR\uc2  executives delivered the news in-person at \uc2 CoolIT\uc2 's headquarters on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 CoolIT\uc2  deal will set a record for payout multiples per salary for employees at \uc2 KKR\uc2 -backed companies, according to \uc2 Pete Stavros\uc2 , \uc2 KKR\uc2 's global co-head of private equity. The payouts are part of a program \uc2 KKR\uc2  has been rolling out across its portfolio companies that gives rank-and-file employees stock on top of their regular wages and benefits. The program is available at 85 companies, affecting almost 200,000 workers, Stavros said.\par \par \uc2 Despite fears that AI will lead to job losses, Stavros said that the \uc2 Ecolab\uc2  deal "has led to an amazing financial outcome for workers."\par \par \uc2 Stavros has formed a nonprofit that \uc2 KKR\uc2  and other private-equity firms have joined to promote broad-based stock ownership at companies. A coalition he assembled is advocating to update a 1974 law to make it easier for workers to own part of their public or private company. A number of politicians from both major parties have started to make the issue a bigger priority ahead of the midterm elections in November.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020260326em3q0001u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
