\par\par \b \uc2 When Driving the Wrong Car To Work Can Get You a Ticket --- Preferred parking at \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  headquarters is reserved for company-made vehicles\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ryan Felton \par \uc2 850 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 March 2026\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 AUBURN HILLS, Mich. -- When employees at \uc2 Jeep\uc2  parent \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  were ordered back to the company's North American headquarters five days a week, they faced challenges familiar to many in the return-to-office era.\par \par \uc2 Working with new colleagues face-to-face, in some cases for the first time. Dodging workplace viruses. Figuring out child-care arrangements.\par \par \uc2 What they likely didn't count on: a parking ticket from their employer because their car wasn't made by \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Employees have said online that \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  security issued them a ticket for parking their vehicles in the wrong spot.\par \par \uc2 "Where do we park if we have non \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  vehicle?" one posted on a \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 -dedicated Reddit page. The answer: Not anywhere you'd like.\par \par \uc2 The crackdown has reignited the debate over a longstanding practice in Detroit, where automakers have encouraged employees to spend their paychecks on company-made vehicles -- with preferential parking as a perk.\par \par \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  parking scofflaws today don't receive a fine and are typically let off with a warning. But if tickets pile up, violators risk getting their vehicles booted by security, leaving them the shame of having to ask a manager to call and get their tires released.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  spokeswoman said preferred parking is reserved for company-branded vehicles. "Employees must adhere to posted signage and communications," she said.\par \par \uc2 The results can be confusing and, at times, amusing. One online user said they were ticketed for parking an Eagle Talon sports car in a \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  lot, despite Eagle being a long-defunct nameplate from Chrysler, which is now owned by \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Seems the security needs a little history lesson," they wrote. The worker didn't respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  said that given the company's long history and broad portfolio of legacy brands, older vehicles may be misidentified by security.\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 Stellantis\uc2  is reviewing its processes to help prevent such situations in the future," the company said. "Employees are encouraged to contact Corporate Security if they believe a parking warning has been issued in error so it can be reviewed and addressed promptly."\par \par \uc2 It's difficult to determine whether ticketing has increased since \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  imposed its return-to-office order. But the concept is rooted in the idea of encouraging carmaker employees to buy what they build.\par \par \uc2 At \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 's headquarters, driving a company vehicle gives workers an appreciable edge, said Al Amici, a former executive who worked there when the company was known as \uc2 Fiat Chrysler\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Several thousand people compete for spots in the lots and decks that encircle headquarters. Depending on where you end up parking, the walk can be as long as 20-30 minutes, Amici said. Tack on another 15-20 minutes to get to your desk, and the motivation for nabbing a closer spot starts to make sense.\par \par \uc2 "There's a strong motivation to park as close to the facility as you can, especially in inclement weather," he said.\par \par \uc2 Crosstown rivals \uc2 General Motors\uc2  and \uc2 Ford Motor\uc2  aren't exempt from the debate. Two decades ago, Ford workers at a Dearborn factory who didn't drive \uc2 Fords\uc2  were banned from parking in a lot adjacent to the facility. The policy spread to other factories, and is still common at auto plants around the country. In 2021, security at a GM plant ticketed a \uc2 Tesla\uc2  owner for parking a "foreign" car in a domestic lot, despite it being made in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 GM declined to comment. A Ford spokesman said the company doesn't designate parking spots for company and competitor vehicles at its corporate facilities.\par \par \uc2 Police in Auburn Hills, where \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 's headquarters is located, said they don't enforce parking regulations on the campus unless someone parks in a handicap space or a fire lane. They haven't received complaints related to any internal enforcement actions, said Deputy Police Chief Scott McGraw.\par \par \uc2 "We are also not aware of any other Auburn Hills-based employers implementing similar brand specific parking requirements," he said.\par \par \uc2 Amici, the former exec, said he understands the motivation for the policy. \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  tries to take the edge off for workers hoofing it from outer perimeter lots, shuttling them in from some locations.\par \par \uc2 "They're trying to strike a balance," he said.\par \par \uc2 The outer perimeter lots seemed orderly on a recent visit. A pair of \uc2 Subaru\uc2  and Hyundai crossovers were parked in spots dedicated for \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  vehicles. No tickets were on their windows.\par \par \uc2 Still, enforcement can be strict. \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  workers heading in and out of the campus said tickets can be spotted on a near-daily basis. Bigger parking decks are often a focal point of the action, they said.\par \par \uc2 One long-tenured employee walking through Lot 11 laughed when asked about the policy. Several years ago, when headquarters was virtually empty, he took a gamble parking in a spot at the end of a row dedicated for Stellantis vehicles.\par \par \uc2 "There was barely anybody there," he said.\par \par \uc2 He got a ticket anyway.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020260326em3q0001p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
