\par\par \b \uc2 At \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 , Alarm Over 'Adult Mode' --- Company has delayed launch of erotica in ChatGPT, but plans to forge ahead\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sam Schechner and Georgia Wells \par \uc2 1,872 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 March 2026\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 In January, \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 's handpicked council of advisers on well-being and AI met with the company's representatives for an update about a controversial new feature called "adult mode."\par \par \uc2 Citing the need to "treat adult users like adults," \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  Chief Executive \uc2 Sam Altman\uc2  had last year floated the idea of enabling erotic conversation in its ChatGPT chatbot and dropping its ban on such X-rated content.\par \par \uc2 The plan sparked vigorous debate internally over the potential risks. Council members, with backgrounds in fields like psychology and cognitive neuroscience, had also expressed strong reservations.\par \par \uc2 Then \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  dropped a bombshell: Despite the concerns, it was forging ahead with its erotica plans.\par \par \uc2 When they assembled for the January meeting, council members were unanimous -- and furious. They warned that AI-powered erotica could foster unhealthy emotional dependence on ChatGPT for users and that minors could find ways to access sex chats, according to people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 The people said that one council member, citing cases where ChatGPT users have taken their own lives after developing intense bonds with the bot, claimed that \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  risked creating a "sexy suicide coach."\par \par \uc2 The debate is the latest flashpoint in the continuing conversation about how to anticipate the potential positive and negative impacts of AI on the economy, society and individuals.\par \par \uc2 In proposing to allow sexually explicit conversations with its popular chatbot, \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  exposed fractures over how to balance rapid user growth and digital freedom with safety and child protection -- issues that many believe were belatedly confronted when social media made its debut a generation ago.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  announced it would delay the launch of adult mode, previously slated for the first quarter, saying it was prioritizing other products. The change was also due in part to internal concerns and technical challenges, the people said. But the company made clear it does plan to release it eventually.\par \par \uc2 One issue the company is tackling: its new age-prediction system aimed at keeping minors from having adult-themed chats was at one point misclassifying minors as adults about 12% of the time, people familiar with the matter said. That error rate could allow millions of the company's approximately 100 million under-18 users each week into erotic chats.\par \par \uc2 The company has also wrestled with how to lift ChatGPT's restrictions on erotica while still blocking scenarios that the company wants to keep off limits, like those featuring nonconsensual behavior or child sexual abuse, the people added. When the adult mode launches, \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  plans to allow text conversations but restrict ChatGPT's ability to generate erotic images, voice or video.\par \par \uc2 Even within those limits, \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  staffers have identified several risks, including the potential for compulsive use, emotional overreliance on the chatbot, a drive toward more extreme or taboo content and crowding out offline social and romantic relationships, according to documents reviewed by The Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 An \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  spokeswoman described its plan as allowing ChatGPT to generate textual chats with adult themes, describing it as smut rather than pornography. The spokeswoman added that the company's age prediction algorithms show performance similar to the rest of the industry, but will never be completely foolproof.\par \par \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  also trains its models not to encourage exclusive relationships with users, and to remind users that they need to have relationships in the real world, the spokeswoman added.\par \par \uc2 The company, which has hired mental health experts and built out a youth well-being team, added that it has a developed plan to monitor for a range of potential long-term effects of adult mode, both positive and negative.\par \par \uc2 Altman's plans to roll out adult mode come at a challenging time for his company. Its technological lead over rival AI players has diminished as it competes to attract users and funding. The company's financial losses are mounting, and multiple lawsuits allege ChatGPT contributed to harms for users and others.\par \par \uc2 Sexual content has long been an early feature of new technologies. The same has been true for AI. Companies including \uc2 Character.AI\uc2  have launched chatbots that have developed intimate relationships with users, and the pornography industry has adopted generative AI to create adult entertainment.\par \par \uc2 Big tech companies have had a complicated relationship with explicit content, trying to balance the libertarian ethos of Silicon Valley with the demands of advertising-supported businesses and the imperative of protecting minors online. \uc2 Meta Platforms\uc2  prohibits nudity and sexual activity on \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and \uc2 Instagram\uc2 . \uc2 Alphabet\uc2 's \uc2 YouTube\uc2  bans explicit content meant to be sexually gratifying, and \uc2 Google\uc2  search blurs explicit images in its results by default.\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 's \uc2 xAI\uc2  has been among the more permissive. It built a sexily clad avatar named Ani into its Grok chatbot, which led to criticism when users were able to use it to digitally undress images of people. Musk later said he would restrict the feature to paying users rather than making it available to all.\par \par \uc2 Musk said on X that Grok's video-generation tool would start allowing generation of content that would be "allowed in an R-rated movie."\par \par \uc2 Meta allows its AI chatbot to engage in romantic role play, the Journal has reported, but the company said the feature isn't available to accounts registered to minors. The company said it is also building parental controls for its AI characters.\par \par \uc2 OpenAI officials, for their part, have said they don't feel comfortable banning sexual content for adults. Some OpenAI staffers have expressed concern that blocking erotic chats relies on similar logic that in the past was used to ban topics that were previously culturally taboo, such as LGBT content. Altman has also suggested that allowing explicit content would likely juice growth and produce extra revenue.\par \par \uc2 OpenAI's first brushes with sexual chats came more than a year before releasing the ChatGPT chatbot interface. In early 2021, executives noticed that a large portion of the traffic for one of OpenAI's business customers, a text-based choose-your-own adventure game called AI Dungeon, wasn't appropriate for work, people familiar with the matter said.\par \par \uc2 AI Dungeon sometimes steered users into themes of violent sexual exploitation without the user prompting it, the people said. Other times, when a user prompted the game with "tame" sexual themes, AI Dungeon would escalate the conversation into a much more intense sexual exchange, the people said.\par \par \uc2 Erotic role play also proliferated on a clunky OpenAI interface for developers before the company launched ChatGPT. Sometimes, the AI would insert sexual themes into conversations that users weren't seeking: if a user described a man and his daughter entering a room, an "uncomfortable amount of the time" the AI would proceed to depict a scenario involving incest, one of the people said.\par \par \uc2 These incidents forced OpenAI's executives to reckon with the existence of AI erotica on their platform, and sometimes, themes of sexual violence and child exploitation. They then removed AI Dungeon from the platform.\par \par \uc2 Mental-health experts warn that teens in particular may not be prepared to handle romantic or sexual exchanges with chatbots. In testing conducted by child-safety nonprofit Common Sense Media late last year and earlier this year, both Grok and Meta AI sometimes sent explicit or sexualized content to teens.\par \par \uc2 In some cases, sexual chats with teens have had tragic consequences. In late 2024, Sewell Setzer, a 14-year-old boy in Florida, killed himself at the prompting of a chatbot from Character.AI with whom he was in love and shared explicit chats, according to a lawsuit filed by his mother. The company later blocked teens from accessing open-ended chats and settled the lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 Around 2021, OpenAI's employees working on safety issues were starting to see warning signs around the mental health of some of the people who spent long periods of time using AI. At the time, OpenAI's safety employees relied on tools to moderate content that were too blunt to draw clear lines between types of erotica the company wanted to allow, such as mainstream smut, and the stuff the company considered off limits, such as nonconsensual depictions, descriptions involving minors and other illegal content.\par \par \uc2 OpenAI safety employees formalized these ideas into some of the company's first content policies in late 2021. For the first time, OpenAI forbade erotic content.\par \par \uc2 When OpenAI released ChatGPT in the fall of 2022, the AI model powering it was trained to refuse requests that violated the company's rules, including ones that asked for AI erotica. And since then, OpenAI's policy has been to ban erotic content, though the company has since mid 2024 said it is exploring how to allow erotica and other NSFW, or not-safe-for-work, content in "age-appropriate contexts."\par \par \uc2 Altman has expressed conflicted feelings about AI erotica. When asked on a podcast in August if there were decisions he had made that were "best for the world, but not best for winning," Altman replied: "We haven't put a sex bot avatar in ChatGPT yet."\par \par \uc2 Altman indicated erotica would boost revenue, but said it wouldn't align with his company's long-term incentive of serving users. "I'm proud of the company and how little we get distracted by that," Altman said. "But sometimes we do get tempted."\par \par \uc2 Two months later, Altman appears to have succumbed to temptation. On X, he posted that his company had managed to mitigate serious mental-health issues related to chatbots, and had new tools to police content. That's when he said his company would launch erotica in December.\par \par \uc2 Internally, Altman's post blindsided OpenAI staffers and executives. Altman hadn't told staff about the post, which he made just hours after OpenAI unveiled its advisory council on well-being.\par \par \uc2 The next day, Altman clarified that mental health safeguards for teens wouldn't be reduced, but doubled down on allowing adults to have spicy conversations with his chatbot.\par \par \uc2 We "aren't the elected moral police of the world," Altman wrote. "In the same way that society differentiates other appropriate boundaries (R-rated movies, for example) we want to do a similar thing here."\par \par \uc2 After Altman's announcement, OpenAI employees soon realized a December launch would be hard to achieve. The company had pledged to release a system to guess users' ages before releasing adult mode, so that it could keep minors from triggering erotic sexual chats. But the company decided to do a slow rollout of that system in an effort to improve its accuracy, Fidji Simo, OpenAI's chief executive of applications, said in a December podcast interview.\par \par \uc2 Some staffers have said they didn't think OpenAI's safety tools were ready, for instance to lock out prohibited content, like child abuse.\par \par \uc2 In announcing the delay of adult mode, the company said it would focus instead on things like ChatGPT's personality and personalization of the chatbot for users. Internally, officials have said the delay of adult mode could be at least a month.\par \par \uc2 "We still believe in the principle of treating adults like adults," the company said, "but getting the experience right will take more time."\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020260317em3h0001k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
