\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 Anthropic\uc2  Standoff Shakes Up AI Talent Race --- Pentagon dispute shows employees seek more than big pay packages\b0\par\par\uc2 By Meghan Bobrowsky \par \uc2 1,058 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 March 2026\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B4\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Anthropic\uc2 's standoff with the \uc2 Defense Department\uc2  has cost it Uncle Sam as a customer, but it brought a momentary advantage in the ferocious talent war between rival artificial-intelligence labs.\par \par \uc2 At least two high-level employees resigned from \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 , citing values and principles, since the company said it reached a deal with the Pentagon to deploy its AI models in classified settings.\par \par \uc2 Anthropic\uc2  was renegotiating its own Pentagon deal and seeking to weave in new safeguards around domestic surveillance and autonomous weapons when talks broke down, prompting the Trump administration to declare the company a supply-chain risk.\par \par \uc2 Caitlin Kalinowski\uc2 , who oversaw hardware within \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 's robotics division, wrote in a post on the social-media platform X over the weekend that she was quitting over the contract.\par \par \uc2 "AI has an important role in national security. But surveillance of Americans without judicial oversight and lethal autonomy without human authorization are lines that deserved more deliberation than they got," she wrote. "This was about principle, not people."\par \par \uc2 In a separate post a few days earlier, Max Schwarzer, a vice president of research at \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 , wrote on X that he was leaving to join \uc2 Anthropic\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Many of [the] people I most trust and respect have joined \uc2 Anthropic\uc2  over the last couple of years, and I'm excited to work with them again. I have also been very impressed with \uc2 Anthropic\uc2 's talent, research taste and values, and I'm excited to be part of what the company does next!" he wrote, adding that he was also leaving to return to individual contributor research work.\par \par \uc2 "We recognize that people have strong views about these issues and we will continue to engage in discussion with employees, government, civil society and communities around the world," a spokeswoman for \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Anthropic\uc2  has seen a surge of public goodwill since Chief Executive \uc2 Dario Amodei\uc2  said the company wouldn't compromise its red lines to do a deal. Its Claude chatbot hit No. 1 in downloads on the \uc2 Apple\uc2  App Store, surpassing \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 's ChatGPT for the first time. San Franciscans chalked messages of appreciation outside its headquarters. Even pop star Katy Perry posted a screenshot of her subscribing to a paid Claude plan with a heart around the page.\par \par \uc2 But no front of competition has mattered more than the red-hot contest for technical talent. And while researchers juggling competing offers have been able to command pay packages worth hundreds of millions of dollars, \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 's recent defections offer a reminder that values have frequently trumped money for the most sought-after prospects.\par \par \uc2 Anthropic\uc2  was founded in 2021 by former \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  researchers, including Amodei, who felt that the company was rushing to build a commercial product without prioritizing safety. Since then, it has cultivated a reputation as a haven for researchers focused on the potential downsides of powerful AI, even as its models established themselves as the preference of a wide range of business customers.\par \par \uc2 "I think leading from values first has kind of allowed us to build a team that really believes in what we're doing," Amodei said last week during a private session at \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2 's Technology, Media & Telecom conference in San Francisco.\par \par \uc2 The Pentagon sought to use \uc2 Anthropic\uc2 's customer relationships as a point of leverage in threatening to declare \uc2 Anthropic\uc2  a supply-chain risk, saying the designation would cut off other \uc2 Defense Department\uc2  contractors from working with the company. But \uc2 Anthropic\uc2  said the status applies only to the work contractors do for the department, and on Monday it sued to challenge the designation. A group of 37 employees of \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  and \uc2 Google DeepMind\uc2  filed a brief asking the court to side with \uc2 Anthropic\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A test of how much \uc2 Anthropic\uc2 's employees care about the company's ethical orientation arrived last summer when \uc2 Meta Platforms\uc2 , seeking to supercharge its model development, mounted an aggressive campaign to woo researchers and engineers from rival labs, including \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  and \uc2 Anthropic\uc2 , dangling compensation packages in some cases worth hundreds of millions of dollars.\par \par \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  countered \uc2 Meta\uc2 's offers with bonuses, and in December, got rid of its vesting cliff, meaning that new employees no longer had to wait for their stock to vest.\par \par \uc2 Anthropic\uc2 , according to Amodei, told employees it wasn't going to alter employees' compensation structure to respond to \uc2 Meta\uc2 's blitz. "The thing we said to everyone was look, you're here for the mission," he said in the \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  session. "We have a system and we're going to hold to that. If you leave, you leave."\par \par \uc2 Anthropic\uc2  ended up losing only two employees to \uc2 Meta\uc2 , versus "several dozen" from \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 , he said. He noted that his company not only has all of its original co-founders but almost all of its first 20 employees.\par \par \uc2 "If you look at our retention rate, it's just the best in the industry," Amodei said. "We're just clearly doing something different."\par \par \uc2 In the days after OpenAI signed its contract with the Pentagon, the company went into damage control mode. Saying the rush to get a deal had "looked opportunistic and sloppy," Chief Executive Sam Altman posted messages on X trying to explain and assuage concerns.\par \par \uc2 Over the weekend following the contract signing, Altman hosted an "ask-me-anything" session on X, where he and two other employees answered questions. And on the next business day, Altman posted that he had been working with the Defense Department to make some additions to the agreement "to make our principles very clear."\par \par \uc2 The following day, Schwarzer resigned. Kalinowski announced she had quit a few days later.\par \par \uc2 "We believe our agreement with the Pentagon creates a workable path for responsible national security uses of AI while making clear our red lines: no domestic surveillance and no autonomous weapons," the OpenAI spokeswoman said.\par \par \uc2 Anthropic isn't immune to scrutiny of its own.\par \par \uc2 An Anthropic safety researcher, Mrinank Sharma, said in early February that he was leaving the company to explore a poetry degree and wrote in a letter to colleagues that the world was in peril from AI.\par \par \uc2 Sharma's decision to leave was related in part to a recent company decision to modify a long-held safety policy, The Wall Street Journal reported.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020260312em3c0001k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
89
