\par\par \b \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  to Open Nashville, Tenn., Office\b0\par\par\uc2 By Heather Haddon \par \uc2 190 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 March 2026\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  is planting its flag in Nashville, Tenn., planning a new corporate office in the city.\par \par \uc2 The coffee chain expects to open the office later this year as part of efforts to expand in parts of the U.S., the company said in an internal message Tuesday. The office will be home to parts of its North American supply-chain operation. The company plans to offer positions to dozens of existing Seattle-based employees to relocate and open additional roles in the market in the future. The company said that Seattle remains its North American and global headquarters. \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  said that its employees who decline to relocate will be eligible for severance and can pursue new roles as they become available.\par \par \uc2 Executives said during an investor event in January that it could add as many as 5,000 U.S. coffeehouses over time. The central, southern and parts of the northeastern U.S. are particular areas of focus, the company has said.\par \par \uc2 Chief Executive \uc2 Brian Niccol\uc2  is shaking up \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  to try to boost sales, and make the company operate more efficiently.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020260304em3400013\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
