\par\par \b \uc2 Papa John's to Shut Hundreds of Shops\b0\par\par\uc2 By Heather Haddon and Connor Hart \par \uc2 240 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 February 2026\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Papa John's International\uc2  said it is closing hundreds of domestic stores, slashing menu items and cutting corporate jobs as it seeks to turnaround its business.\par \par \uc2 The fourth-largest pizza chain by U.S. sales plans to close 300 stores by the end of 2027. Most of the locations, which are owned by franchisees, will close this year.\par \par \uc2 Shares of \uc2 Papa John's\uc2  fell 8.6% Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Chief Executive \uc2 Todd Penegor\uc2  said Thursday the company reviewed all of its North American restaurants and identified restaurants where sales patterns had changed and would need a lot of investment. The company said those sites are largely unprofitable and generate low sales.\par \par \uc2 Papa Johns\uc2  is in the midst of a turnaround as the overall pizza sector struggles to increase sales. Pizza Hut owner \uc2 Yum Brands\uc2  is currently exploring a sale of the brand. Pizza Hut plans to close around 250 underperforming U.S. locations this year.\par \par \uc2 Papa Johns\uc2  has also considered strategic alternatives for the business, including a potential sale. As part of a turnaround effort, the company said that had reduced its corporate workforce by roughly 7%. A menu revamp is planned, too. Fourth-quarter profit fell 42% from a year earlier to $8.6 million. Revenue fell 6.1% to $498.2 million, missing analysts' forecasts. Stripping out one-time costs, earnings were 34 cents a share.\par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw262\pich444\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3930\pichgoal6660
