\par\par \b \uc2 First Brands Lays Off Employees --- The company told workers several potential financing sources fell through\b0\par\par\uc2 By Alicia McElhaney \par \uc2 384 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 February 2026\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 First Brands Group\uc2  has been unable to find financing or a buyer to continue most of its companywide operations, the bankrupt auto-parts supplier said as it laid off employees in its aftermarket businesses Monday.\par \par \uc2 First Brands\uc2  said in a letter to laid-off workers that several potential buyers for the company "suddenly and unexpectedly" withdrew or narrowed their bids to interest in certain units in recent days.\par \par \uc2 "While certain outside parties did ultimately decide to fund specific business lines, the company was unfortunately unable to receive any commitment to fund companywide operations," said the letter, a copy of which was reviewed by WSJ Pro Bankruptcy.\par \par \uc2 The company has been teetering on the brink of liquidation for weeks and surviving on emergency financing from automotive customers after its lenders declined to put more money in.\par \par \uc2 First Brands\uc2  filed for chapter 11 in September as restructuring advisers found the company had double-pledged receivables and made up invoices to use as collateral. The scale of the company's accounting problems became clear only after it filed for bankruptcy, and the $1.1 billion in financing it received from debtor-in-possession lenders ran out.\par \par \uc2 Last month, \uc2 First Brands\uc2  said it would shut down parts of its North American business. The wind-down of those businesses, including aftermarket parts maker Cardone and spark-plug manufacturer Autolite, comes in addition to the layoffs announced Monday.\par \par \uc2 Customers including Ford, \uc2 General Motors\uc2  and \uc2 Harley-Davidson\uc2  stepped in to provide a last-minute lifeline for the company -- week-to-week financing to cover costs associated with products crucial for their vehicles. The original-equipment business lines that serve these customers at \uc2 First Brands\uc2  will remain open.\par \par \uc2 However, \uc2 First Brands\uc2  was unable to receive any further financing to fund other operations, and several prospective lenders decided to reduce or cease their funding, the company's letter to employees said. As a result, the sale of certain facilities and ongoing operations of the company can't move ahead as expected.\par \par \uc2 First Brands\uc2  has been in court-overseen mediation with its lenders. On Monday, Judge Christopher Lopez in Houston ordered them to conclude mediation efforts by midday Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 Alicia McElhaney writes for WSJ Pro Bankruptcy.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020260224em2o0001y\par }\par \b \uc2 Search Summary\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Date\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/20